course: dictionary
lesson: 3506
title: Fasten: close, join or fix
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Fasten is a verb, a doing word. It means to close, join or fix something so it stays shut or in place. Think of a zip, a button or a buckle: when you fasten it, it holds. Fastens, fastened and fastening are the same word in different forms.
explain: Context tells you which meaning you need. «Keeping your seat belt fastened whenever you are seated protects you» means the belt is closed and holding you in place. It does not mean the belt is quick or speedy.
explain: Fasten can also mean to fix your eyes or attention on something. A story might say «Her eyes fastened on the door», which means she stared at it and could not look away. Ask yourself: is something being closed, or is someone's gaze being fixed? The clues will tell you.
fact: Fasten is a verb. Fastens, fastened and fastening are its other forms.
fact: «Fasten» means to close, join or fix something so it stays shut or in place.
fact: «Fasten your seatbelt» is a safety instruction. A fastened seat belt keeps you safely in your seat.
fact: On a plane, your seat belt should stay fastened whenever you are seated, because sudden bumps called turbulence can happen.
fact: «Fasten» can also mean to attach one thing to another, or to fix your eyes on something.
exercise: «Keeping your seat belt fastened whenever you are seated protects you.» What does fastened mean here? | Sung loudly | Loosened and dropped | Painted bright red | *Closed and held in place
exercise: «Her eyes fastened on the door.» What does fasten mean here? | Forgot all about it | Ran out through it | Opened it quickly | *Stared at it and could not look away
exercise: Dad says, «Fasten your helmet strap before you ride.» What should you do? | Throw the helmet away | *Close it and fix it so it stays on | Wash the strap in the sea | Ignore the strap
test: Yesterday Mia ___ her coat and ran outside. Which word fits best? | *fastened | fasten | fastens | fastening
test: «Fasten the gate so the sheep stay in.» What does fasten mean here? | Paint the gate blue | *Close it so it stays shut | Count the sheep | Take the gate off
exam: Which of these means attach one thing to another? | Dance around the room | Read a book quietly | *Fasten the label to the box | Sing a happy song
